ONNX Runtime provides a shared C API and C++ wrappers for ONNX model inference.
This EmberBSD profile uses the CPU execution provider and standard operators.
On NetBSD, device discovery also reports DRM-backed GPUs via /dev/dri and PCI
config ioctls so the WebGPU EP can bind without the software-adapter escape
hatch. With the webgpu package option it also ships the shared WebGPU plugin
(libonnxruntime_providers_webgpu.so) built against Dawn (Vulkan backend only)
using the ORT 1.31 Dawn pin. Training, Python bindings, contrib/ML operators,
telemetry and CUDA/ROCm/OpenVINO/TensorRT are disabled. Upstream Python
generators run only during the build.
